  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "is/oIa36h5IBPJjN+9zt11xRILA=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:33:24.233Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "Sopra Steria UK carries Microsoft and Salesforce as its recorded platforms, against public, banking and insurance verticals. Its do-not-pitch tier came from a mechanical rescore of a provisional v2 tail entry on size and slot occupancy, with no v3 evidence pass and an OSS-portfolio screen still outstanding.\n\nThe row is most informative read against its Dutch sibling, which shares the recorded stack but adds warnings about unseparable revenue and an unstable org chart. The UK entry has neither, which means the two national rows were assessed independently even though they belong to one group \u2014 and that the caveats on the Dutch row are specifically about its integration, not about Sopra Steria generally.\n\nOn its own the UK row asserts little: two large proprietary platforms occupying the slot, and a tier derived from scale. Both point the same way, but neither was verified against the firm's actual portfolio.\n\n---\n\n## Leads sharing this finding (1)\n\n**9 \u00b7 do not pitch**\n- Sopra Steria UK (UK)\n\nVerbatim research text this claim was extracted from:\n\n> DERIVED, NOT SCORED ON v3 \u2014 v2 row rescored mechanically (size + slot-occupancy only). Run the OSS-portfolio screen before acting. v2 verticals: Public, banking, insurance",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-19T11:33:24.233889Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-19T11:33:24.233894Z"
    }
  },
